.TH ZAVA 1 "2026" "zava 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zava \- console-based audio visualizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zava
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zava
is a console audio visualizer: it captures PCM audio from an input device,
runs it through a dual-buffer FFT, and draws a spectrum as sub-character
Unicode blocks in the terminal.
.PP
It is a from-scratch Rust reimplementation of CAVA
.RI ( https://github.com/karlstav/cava )
with the same DSP pipeline, configuration semantics and rendering behaviour,
plus an interactive settings menu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-config " \fIPATH\fR"
Read configuration from
.IR PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-test
Use a synthetic in-process test signal instead of real audio. Useful for
checking layout and colours without playing anything.
.TP
.BI \-\-method " METHOD"
Override the audio input method. One of
.IR pipewire ", " pulse ", " alsa ", " fifo ", " cpal ", " test .
.TP
.BI \-\-source " SOURCE"
Override the input device; for
.B fifo
this is the path of the named pipe.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " METHOD"
Override the output method. One of
.IR noncurses ", " ncurses ", " raw .
.TP
.BI \-\-channels " MODE"
Override the output channel layout:
.B stereo
or
.BR mono .
.TP
.B \-\-generate\-config
Write a configuration file to the standard location (or to
.BR \-p \fIPATH\fR
if given) and exit. Existing values are preserved; missing keys are appended.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help summary and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Up / Down
Increase / decrease sensitivity by 15%.
.TP
.B Left / Right
Fewer / more bars. In auto mode
.RB ( bars " = 0)"
this widens / narrows each bar; with a fixed
.B bars
it changes the count. Both stop at the limit that fits the terminal unless
.B wrap_bars
is enabled.
.TP
.B m
Open the interactive settings menu. Navigate with
.BR Up / Down ,
adjust the highlighted row with
.BR Left / Right
and leave with
.BR m ", " q " or " Esc .
.TP
.B o
Cycle the orientation live:
.IR bottom ", " top ", " left ", " right ", " horizontal .
.TP
.B r
Reload the configuration file.
.TP
.B c
Reload colours only.
.TP
.B f / b
Cycle the foreground / background colour.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zava/config
.TQ
.I ~/.config/zava/config
Configuration file.
.B zava
is config-isolated: it never reads or writes
.IR ~/.config/cava/config .
If a legacy CAVA config exists a warning is printed and it is ignored.
.TP
.I /usr/share/zava/config.example
Fully commented reference configuration installed by the package.
.SH ORIENTATIONS
.TP
.B bottom
Bars grow up from the bottom edge.
.TP
.B top
Bars grow down from the top edge.
.TP
.B left
Bars grow right, from the left edge.
.TP
.B right
Bars grow left, from the right edge.
.TP
.B horizontal
Classic bottom-up bars with the block always centred on the horizontal axis.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with the default monitor:
.PP
.RS 4
zava
.RE
.PP
Check the rendering with a synthetic signal:
.PP
.RS 4
zava \-\-test
.RE
.PP
Visualize a FIFO fed by another program:
.PP
.RS 4
zava \-\-method fifo \-\-source /tmp/music.fifo
.RE
.PP
Emit raw data for another program to consume:
.PP
.RS 4
zava \-\-output raw
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cava (1)
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.IR https://github.com/<you>/zava/issues .
